# Belenios 3.0, section 4.15: proof that a ciphertext (alpha, beta)
# encrypts a non-zero value.  www.belenios.org/specification.pdf
#
# The prover publishes A0 = beta^s * y^(-s*r) and proves that A0, in
# base (beta, y), has the same representation as 1 does in base
# (alpha, g).  Writing u = s and v = -s*r, that is the two equations
# below -- and the first of them has the identity as its target.
secrets u v
claims  u v
eq  1    alpha  g
eq  A0   beta   y
